{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/how-we-protected-the-uk-and-space-in-february-2026","content_id":"4ede3ebe-9dbf-4819-9dcc-f0255b60b96d","description":"This report was issued in March 2026 and covers the time period 1 February 2026 to 28 February 2026 inclusive.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>February saw sustained levels of space activity, with higher levels of uncontrolled re-entries but lower levels of collision alerts and space weather activity than in January.</p>\n\n<p>All  NSpOC warning and protection services were functioning throughout the period.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"re-entry-analysis\">Re-entry analysis</h2>\n<p>February saw an increase in the number of objects re-entering Earth’s atmosphere, monitored by NSpOC, when compared with the previous month.</p>\n\n<p>Of the 66 objects that re-entered, 59 were satellites, 6 were rocket bodies and one was likely a piece of debris.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"image embedded\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba769d0736dc1920e7f5a0/Re-entry_Manual.svg\" alt=\"\"></div>\n<figcaption><p>March: 85, April: 92, May: 64, June: 55, July: 52, August: 34, September: 39, October: 54, November: 43, December: 52, January: 50, February: 66</p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2 id=\"collision-avoidance-analysis\">Collision avoidance analysis</h2>\n<p>Collision risks to UK-licensed satellites were lower in February than in January.</p>\n<figure class=\"image embedded\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba769def857f1696d12585/Collision_Avoidance_manual.svg\" alt=\"\"></div>\n<figcaption><p>March: 2,588, April: 2,620, May: 1,546, June: 1,259, July: 1,038, August: 971, September: 1,537, October: 2,402, November: 2,472, December: 2,643, January: 2,608, February: 2,117</p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<h2 id=\"registered-space-objects-rsos-analysis\">Registered Space Objects (RSOs) analysis</h2>\n<p>The in-orbit population increased in February, with a net addition of 244 objects to the US Satellite Catalogue.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"image embedded\"><div class=\"img\"><img src=\"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba769d530e305110e7f59e/RSO_Manual__NEW_.svg\" alt=\"\"></div>\n<figcaption><p>March: 30,183, April: 30,311, May: 30,560, June: 30,885, July: 31,093, August: 31,347, September, 31,636, October: 31,928, November: 32,306, December: 32,694, January: 32,921, February: 33,165</p></figcaption></figure>\n\n<p>The number of Resident Space Objects (RSOs) reported may be subject to small adjustments over time as the way objects are tracked is refined. Figures in this report reflect the most current available data and may differ slightly from those published in previous months.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"fragmentation-analysis\">Fragmentation analysis</h2>\n<p>There have been no new fragmentation (break-up) incidents this month.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"space-weather-analysis\">Space weather analysis</h2>\n<p>A reduction in space weather activity was observed during the month of February, with some geomagnetic storms and solar flares registered throughout the month.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"comments\">Comments</h2>\n<p>The National Space Operations Centre combines and coordinates UK civil and military space domain awareness capabilities to enable operations, promote prosperity and protect UK interests in space and on Earth from space-related threats, risks and hazards.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-03-19T14:54:42Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["6b681c1a-a04b-40fa-bddd-d331c2f730e2","1a22a221-513b-4a8d-ae97-e3668b6d5568","d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","cb2b9743-d253-40c1-a037-c5770a7b90cd"],"images":[{"caption":"The National Space Operations Centre is led by the UK Space Agency and UK Space Command in partnership with the Met Office.","content_type":"image/png","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764c6b1db9df335fcaec/s216_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764c7c81ce194cd12589/s300_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764c7c81ce194cd1258a/s465_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764c815be18dfd5fcaee/s630_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764cef857f1696d12584/s712_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ba764c6b1db9df335fcaed/s960_NSpOC_GDS_Image_White_Large.png"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"news_story","first_published_at":"2026-03-19T14:54:42+00:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/how-we-protected-the-uk-and-space-in-february-2026","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/how-we-protected-the-uk-and-space-in-february-2026","base_path":"/government/news/how-we-protected-the-uk-and-space-in-february-2026","content_id":"4ede3ebe-9dbf-4819-9dcc-f0255b60b96d","document_type":"news_story","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-03-19T14:54:42Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"How we protected the UK and space in February 2026","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/how-we-protected-the-uk-and-space-in-february-2026","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"OT1409","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/national-space-operations-centre","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/national-space-operations-centre","base_path":"/government/organisations/national-space-operations-centre","content_id":"6b681c1a-a04b-40fa-bddd-d331c2f730e2","details":{"acronym":"NSpOC","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":null,"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"National Space<br/>Operati